      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The township’s official erection was confirmed March 19, 1875, and the first election was held May 11, 1875 at Samuel Hullihan’s public house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pagenweb.org/~clearfield/individual%20twnsps/greenwood.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Greenwood sits in southern Crawford County, directly south of Mercer County, and its northern edge follows the Conneaut Outlet wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenwoodtwpcrawfordpa.gov/about-our-township/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The township covers 36.6 square miles, almost all land, with only 0.19 square miles of water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenwoodtwpcrawfordpa.gov/about-our-township/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Governance is handled by three elected Township Supervisors, each serving six‑year terms with elections every other year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenwoodtwpcrawfordpa.gov/about-our-township/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The township employs three full‑time road workers and a part‑time secretary to maintain its roads.",
